            <div xml:id="d1132">

                <pb facs="1027" n="713" xml:id="pg713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111W74/3</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Buckner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-14T18:00:00-00:43">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1914, 6 pm.</hi>
                    </date>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>French Government demands that German wireless be closed or neutrality would not
                    be observed according to the Hague Convention V, 1907, Articles 3, 5, and 25.
                    French wireless still open. Liberian Government desires advice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buckner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
